# --- RE-STAMPED 2026-07-27 (WI-337) - on the LINE-ENDING-NORMALIZED basis ----
# Supersedes the WI-334 re-stamp of the same day, which was INVALID.
#
# HISTORICAL, NON-REPRODUCIBLE (marked under WI-342): the 28/9 split below was
# counted on the working tree as it stood before WI-337 normalized it. That tree
# is gone and no manifest of the nine files was kept, so this specific figure
# cannot be re-derived - `git ls-files --eol` on any later checkout answers a
# different question. What IS checkable, and what the conclusion rests on: the
# 164-entry census WI-334 committed, and that the same corpus under uniform LF
# *and* uniform CRLF yields 208 (128-REVIEW-A reproduced both).
#
# WI-334 regenerated this census on a Windows working tree whose scripts/ was
# MIXED - 28 files LF, 9 CRLF: the residue of editing on Windows after an
# `eol=lf` checkout, not of the checkout itself. check_dupes tokenized those
# bytes (a NEWLINE token's text is "\r\n" on one and "\n" on the other), so a
# fingerprint was a property of the CHECKOUT, and two files with different
# endings could not match each other AT ALL. The result was not merely
# mis-fingerprinted, it was a different and WRONG SET: 164 blocks, where the
# same corpus under uniform line endings has 208. A fresh LF worktree therefore
# reported 128 unsanctioned blocks, and `dupes` is a G3-only step at a derived
# G3 gate - the first hosted CI run would have red.
#
# WI-337 normalizes line endings before tokenizing (`normalized_source()`), so a
# fingerprint is now a property of the CODE. Guarded by
# tests/test_check_dupes.py::test_emitted_census_is_identical_under_lf_and_crlf
# plus test_normalization_is_what_makes_the_census_portable, which mutates the
# normalization away and asserts the census then diverges.
#
# What this re-stamp IS - measured, not asserted:
#   * 208 blocks, verified IDENTICAL in this CRLF working tree and in a fresh LF
#     worktree (the two environments that disagreed).
#   * 191 of the 208 were ALREADY SANCTIONED by the pre-WI-334 census at
#     1b65c4d - the LF-based one, i.e. the basis hosted CI actually uses. So
#     this is a RESTORATION of that basis, not a new blanket sanction.
#   * 17 are drift since 1b65c4d: blocks whose tokens moved under WI-333's ruff
#     fixes, WI-334's gen_open_items extraction, and WI-337's own edit to
#     check_dupes.py. Read rather than counted, they are the established F5
#     families - the per-script CLI preamble, `load_csv`/`refs`, the `_git`
#     subprocess wrapper, the stack-profile reader - plus known intra-module
#     WI-280 debt in gen_trajectory / trace / check_trajectory.
#
# This re-stamp deliberately made NO classification claim. WI-334's signed claim
# that "MOST" of its blocks were the deliberate CLI preamble was REFUTED by
